    rationale:
      "AGENT_PROTOCOL is not a changelog — it is the one file every autonomous agent working this repo is instructed to read in full before starting any task. Unlike ITERATIONS/BUSINESS_DECISIONS (which trade size for a complete audit trail on purpose), a bloated rulebook has a real, recurring cost: every future agent burns context reading redundant historical narrative before it can find the still-binding rule, and a rule buried in a wall of superseded detail is more likely to be missed. The chosen alternative — leaving it uncapped and growing indefinitely, or display-capping it like the /docs/process page — was rejected: an agent needs the FULL rulebook (not 'the most recent N rules'), so the fix has to be content consolidation, not a display window. Every entry outside the two identified chains (cooperation workflow, dual-backend, money/ledger, security/injection, testing, product data-model, docs/stack, and several already-compact specific rules) was deliberately left untouched — this is a targeted trim of demonstrated redundancy, not a wholesale rewrite.",
