      "Same bug class daily-digest-button-item-count-drift fixed in a different component, found immediately after by a follow-up research subagent seeded toward the same client-side blind spot on the next empty-backlog run. The Commerce payouts (manual) panel's list body only ever renders commercePayoutsByLead — summarizeCommerceOrdersByLead(commerceOrders) filtered through commerceOrdersByLeadSummaryNeedsAttention (a lead needs attention only if unpaidCount > 0 or it has a clawback-needed order) — but the panel's header badge showed the length of the pre-filter `commerceOrders` prop itself (mergeCommerceOrdersForReview(listUnpaidCommerceOrders(), listCommerceOrdersRefunded(), listCommerceOrdersDisputed())), the same 'header count from the pre-slice array, not the rendered one' mistake. A Buy now order that was refunded or disputed before it was ever marked paid out owes the client nothing (isCommerceOrderRefunded/isCommerceOrderDisputed exclude it from unpaidTotalUsd, and commerceOrderNeedsClawback requires paidOutAt to already be set, which it isn't) — so its lead's summary correctly fails commerceOrdersByLeadSummaryNeedsAttention and never appears in the list. But that order still arrives in the merged review feed (mergeCommerceOrdersForReview explicitly includes every refunded/disputed order regardless of payout status, by design, so a clawback-needed order — refunded or disputed AFTER payout — isn't missed). The net effect: every ordinary, fully-resolved refund/dispute a Commerce client's shoppers generate over time permanently and silently inflates the header's order count, while the visible list below shrinks back down to just the leads genuinely needing operator action — a trust-eroding drift in the one dashboard panel meant to prevent an operator from double-paying a client or missing a real clawback. Independently re-verified against current source (not the subagent's report) before fixing: read src/lib/commerce/orders.ts's summarizeCommerceOrdersByLead/commerceOrdersByLeadSummaryNeedsAttention/commerceOrderNeedsClawback definitions and src/app/dashboard/leads/page.tsx's commerceOrdersForPayoutsPanel wiring to confirm the merged feed genuinely includes orders whose lead-summary gets filtered out, then confirmed leads-client.tsx's header literally read `commerceOrders.length` (the raw prop) rather than anything derived from commercePayoutsByLead. Fixed by adding a small, reusable pure helper (mirroring the daily-digest fix's 'compute the displayed total once, from the same data the render loop already uses' approach) rather than inlining a `.reduce()` at the JSX call site, so a future sibling consumer (e.g. a digest section for Commerce payouts, if one is ever added) can reuse the same derivation instead of re-summing ad hoc. Verified: npm test (full suite, see ITERATIONS for exact count), npm run lint, npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json, npm run build, and a dev-server sanity check of /dashboard/leads — see the matching ITERATIONS entry for exact pass/fail counts.",
