      "A dispatched research subagent (Convex/SQLite parity + sold-capability tier of the empty-backlog cooperation priority order, explicitly steered away from re-reporting today's already-fixed inquiry-id-collision-guard) found leads-client.tsx's notesEditSlug/notesDraft state pair is a single, non-keyed draft slot — the exact same shape commerceEditSlug/commerceDraftItems had before commerce-draft-items-cross-lead-clobber fixed it earlier today for the Commerce catalog editor. openNotesEditor(lead, reason) unconditionally calls setNotesEditSlug(lead.slug) and setNotesDraft(lead.notes ?? \"\"), with no check for whether a DIFFERENT lead's editor is already open with unsaved text. That's safe at its one manual call site (the per-row notes button toggles the SAME row's own editor by construction), but not at its two soft auto-prompt call sites: shouldPromptNotesAfterStageChange fires whenever any lead's stage newly enters discovery_call, and shouldPromptNotesAfterOutreachStep fires whenever any lead's Email 3 outreach step lands — both are ordinary background pipeline progress on lead B that can happen while an operator is mid-draft on lead A's notes in a completely unrelated part of the same dashboard page. Concrete failure path independently re-verified against current source before fixing (not the subagent's report as ground truth): read the full state block (leads-client.tsx) and confirmed notesEditSlug/notesDraft/notesPromptReason are plain useState, not keyed per-lead; read openNotesEditor (unconditional overwrite, no current-slug check) and closeNotesEditor; read handleStageChange's success path and confirmed shouldPromptNotesAfterStageChange(previousStage, newStage) directly gates an unconditional openNotesEditor(current, \"discovery_call\") call with `current` being the LEAD JUST STAGE-CHANGED, not whichever lead's editor (if any) is open; read handleSendFollowUp and confirmed the identical shape for shouldPromptNotesAfterOutreachStep/openNotesEditor(current, \"email_3\"); read notes.ts's own doc comment on notesPromptMessage ('never blocks stage/email success') confirming the prompt is explicitly meant to be a low-stakes soft nudge, not something that should ever have a destructive side effect on unrelated in-progress operator work. Confirmed via grep across AGENT_PROTOCOL's full text that no existing rule already covers this — the closest is the generic 'extract event-handler logic into a pure function for Vitest coverage' testing-convention note (methodology, not this specific instance), and commerce-draft-items-cross-lead-clobber's own ITERATIONS entry explicitly scoped itself to the commerce catalog editor only, never touching the notes editor. Chose the editingSlug-must-match guard shape (mirroring commerceDraftItemsAfterSync's editingSlug/syncedSlug comparison) over alternatives considered: (a) keying notesDraft per-lead in a Map/Record — rejected as unnecessary scope growth for a single-editor-at-a-time UI pattern where only one row's editor can be visibly open at once; (b) prompting the operator to confirm losing the current draft before auto-switching — rejected because the auto-prompt is explicitly a soft, dismissible nudge ('Skip for now' already exists) triggered by an action the operator took on a DIFFERENT row, and forcing a blocking confirm dialog on background pipeline progress would be a worse UX regression than silently not-stealing-focus; the guard's effect is simply that the soft prompt no-ops when it would clobber, exactly matching notesPromptMessage's own 'never blocks' contract — the underlying stage-change/follow-up-send action always still succeeds regardless of whether the notes prompt fires. New tests in notes.test.ts: shouldAutoOpenNotesEditor allows opening when nothing is open; allows a lead re-opening/refreshing its own already-open editor; blocks stealing a different lead's open editor (direct regression case for the clobber). Verified: npm test (2149 passed, 166 files = prior 2146 baseline + 3 new, all in notes.test.ts) + npm run lint (clean) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run build (tsc clean, all 31 routes generated) + npm run dev sanity check: curled /, /dashboard/leads, /preview/demo-cafe, /docs/process (all 200; grepped the dashboard HTML for error-boundary markers — none), then stopped the dev server and confirmed no next-server process remained (port 3000 free).",
